{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112228","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112228/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112228/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112228/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112228","id":3572884203,"node_id":"I_kwDOAO6SJc7U9eLr","number":112228,"title":"Edge / outline artifacts when using roughness and nearest-filter normal maps","user":{"login":"liljohn360","id":8534384,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MzQzODQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8534384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360","html_url":"https://github.com/liljohn360","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1609442062,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjA5NDQyMDYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:shaders","name":"topic:shaders","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-10-31T00:05:46Z","updated_at":"2025-10-31T08:30:01Z","closed_at":"2025-10-31T00:30:11Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.5.1 stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot 4.5.1 Stable - RTX 3070Ti - Forward +\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm working on a pixel art style 3D game, which necessitates low resolution, nearest-filtered images, including normal maps. I noticed that creating pixel art normal maps and using them on reflective (low roughness) surfaces produces a grid-like outline artifact that's rather unpleasant.\n\nThinking this was a texture sampling issue, I used a procedural checker texture and the artifact is still present.\n\nDisabling \"Screen Space Roughness Limiter\" reduces the artifact, but it never completely goes away.\n\nI tried combing through the scene_forward shader source, but other than the roughness limiter I'm struggling to see where this could be coming from.\n\n<img width=\"1031\" height=\"684\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/89e84b97-2d55-436a-9847-19469d78c8b6\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUse a nearest-filtered normal map that's quite low resolution, or a procedural checkerboard texture as a normal map, then turn down the roughness. On the pixels at the boundary between these two values, a grid-like edge artifact is clearly visible.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[new_game_project_2025-10-30_23-55-39.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23247262/new_game_project_2025-10-30_23-55-39.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"clayjohn","id":1652133